Found in k198. The comment on UnrealConfig.Unattended, the log line in run() and README "Crashes & recovery" say -unattended suppresses both recovery prompts (README: checked against the UE 5.7 source, no file named). Epic's flag reference lists a separate flag, AutoDeclinePackageRecovery, and the cleanRecovery comment itself says the restore dialog would block an unattended restart. skills/unreagent-iterate repeats the claim.

Needs a Windows run with an editor first: experiment U2 in docs/research/2026-11-21-unreal-editor.md. Then either add the documented flag to the default editor args, or correct the comments, README and the shipped skill. Owner after the run: unreagent-worker (code), unreagent-doc-writer and unreagent-skill-author for the text.

From the k206/k210 review (2026-11-21): the shipped skills no longer state the claim. The log line at cmd/launcher/main.go:214 ('no crash dialog, no recovery prompt') and the comment at internal/config/config.go:91-92 are now the only places that do.

Windows run 2026-11-22 (U2, package-recovery part), UE 5.7.4 (CL 51494982) and 5.8.4 (CL 58902052), both Launcher builds; Windows 11 Pro 26H2 build 26300.9711. Disposable Blueprint project from TP_BlankBP (PythonScriptPlugin as a control channel, autosave set to 1 min), editor started directly, not through unreagent. Raw timelines, stdout and editor logs: C:\Temp\unreagent-probe\runs\03..09 (5.7) and 20..24 (5.8) on that machine.

Setup: open /Game/ProbeMap, spawn 3 PointLights (map dirty), wait for the autosave (came 58 s later, also under -unattended), TerminateProcess the editor. State then: Saved/Autosaves/PackageRestoreData.json = {"RestoreEnabled": true, "Packages": [{"PackagePathName": "/Game/ProbeMap", "PackageAssetName": "ProbeMap", "AutoSavePath": "Game/ProbeMap_Auto1.umap"}]} plus Saved/Autosaves/Game/ProbeMap_Auto1.umap. Every variant started from a copy of exactly that state. Same results on 5.7.4 and 5.8.4:
- no flag: modal window "Pakete wiederherstellen" (German UI; Restore Packages) ~10.5 s after start; no game-thread tick for 120-150 s, i.e. the editor blocks until a human answers.
- -unattended: no prompt, first tick ~14 s, NOT restored (0 PointLights). The restore file is left untouched during the session and is rewritten to {"RestoreEnabled": false, "Packages": []} only at the clean exit (exit 0).
- -AutoDeclinePackageRecovery alone: no prompt, not restored; the file is cleared to RestoreEnabled false at start (~12 s, before the first tick).
- both flags: exactly like -unattended alone: file not cleared at start, only at the clean exit. Next to -unattended the flag had no visible effect.
- chain (5.7): restore state, start with -unattended, TerminateProcess before anything got dirty -> file still holds the old entry -> a later start without flags shows the restore prompt again, for the autosave of two sessions back.
More file facts: PackageRestoreData.json exists after every clean exit (96 bytes, RestoreEnabled false); UTF-16LE without BOM, CRLF, tab-indented; the editor rewrites it to RestoreEnabled true, Packages [] as soon as a package gets dirty (so a stale entry is dropped at the session's first dirty package) and lists packages after an autosave; the autosave .umap stays behind as an orphan after a clean exit. LogPackageAutoSaver at VeryVerbose logged nothing. Both flags exist as strings in UnrealEditor-UnrealEd.dll 5.7.4.

Verdict:
- "-unattended suppresses the recovery prompt" (comment on UnrealConfig.Unattended, run() log line): CONFIRMED for package recovery on 5.7.4 and 5.8.4. Disaster recovery (Concert) was not tested.
- README "Crashes & recovery": "discards the unclean state instead of asking" is CONTRADICTED in part: -unattended skips the restore but keeps the state until a clean exit or the first dirty package; a crash before that hands the old offer to the next start without -unattended. "not re-checked for UE 5.8" can go: 5.8.4 is now checked.
- cleanRecovery comment "its restore dialog would block an unattended restart": does not hold with -unattended (no dialog); it holds only for unattended: false.
- research doc section 1 row on AutoDeclinePackageRecovery: -unattended does not do the same; it suppresses and skips, it does not decline (does not clear the state).
Decision proposed for the owners: do NOT add -AutoDeclinePackageRecovery to the default args (no effect next to -unattended); correct the comment at internal/config/config.go:91-92, the log line at cmd/launcher/main.go:214 and the README to the observed behaviour. Optional: with unattended: false, -AutoDeclinePackageRecovery would be the way to drop a stale offer without a prompt. Not run: the missing-module part of U2 (on k208 as U5).

